body:
**`NodeLabels` should be deep-copied in `Clone()`**

Since `NodeLabels` is a `map[string]string`, the `Clone()` method needs to deep-copy it. Currently `Clone()` does `cloned := *n` which copies the map header, so original and clone share the same underlying map — a data race if one goroutine reads the clone while another writes to the original.

`VirtualNodeQuotaArray` (a slice) is already handled defensively with a deep copy. Apply the same pattern to `NodeLabels`:
```go
if n.NodeLabels != nil {
    cloned.NodeLabels = make(map[string]string, len(n.NodeLabels))
    for k, v := range n.NodeLabels {
        cloned.NodeLabels[k] = v
    }
}
```

