**Suggestion (testability):** The annotation-promotion logic on lines 136–141 (both `HOSTDIR_MOUNT_KEY` and `KERNEL_CMDLINE_APPEND_KEY`) lives inside the `create_sandbox` closure and has no test coverage. Consider extracting it into a pure function like:

```rust
fn promote_metadata_keys(
    mut meta: HashMap<String, String>,
    annotations: &mut HashMap<String, String>,
) -> HashMap<String, String> {
    if let Some(value) = meta.remove(HOSTDIR_MOUNT_KEY) {
        annotations.insert(HOSTDIR_MOUNT_KEY.to_string(), value);
    }
    if let Some(value) = meta.remove(KERNEL_CMDLINE_APPEND_KEY) {
        annotations.insert(KERNEL_CMDLINE_APPEND_KEY.to_string(), value);
    }
    meta
}
```

This makes the promotion logic trivially testable with focused unit tests (e.g., key present, key absent, empty value, both keys simultaneously), and also improves readability by isolating the transformation from the surrounding closure/request-building code.

