body:
**Suggestion:** Add a defensive bounds check at the top of `setFeature`.

If `setFeature` is ever called with `idx >= total` (i.e., `blockIdx >= blocks`), the slice indexing on the following line will cause an out-of-bounds panic and crash the process. Currently the only caller (`enableTXTCPMangleIDSegmentation`) always passes consistent `idx`/`total` from the same `featureIndex` call, so this is a latent rather than active risk. A simple early return with `fmt.Errorf` makes this robust against future refactoring:

```go
if idx >= total {
    return fmt.Errorf("feature index %d out of range (total features: %d)", idx, total)
}
```

