body:
**Suggestion:** Add a double-check after acquiring the write lock in `featureIndex` to prevent redundant ioctl work under concurrent access. When two goroutines simultaneously miss the cache, both issue the same `ETHTOOL_GSSET_INFO` + `ETHTOOL_GSTRINGS` ioctl sequence. Adding a brief check after the Lock would eliminate this waste:

```go
featureIndexCacheMu.Lock()
if _, already := featureIndexCache[name]; !already {
    featureIndexCache[name] = featureIndexCacheEntry{idx: i, total: n}
}
featureIndexCacheMu.Unlock()
```

This is a minor optimization since the function is called infrequently (once per tap creation), but it follows Go best practices for lazy-init caches.

