body:
**Security: Unchecked float64 to int64 overflow on multiplication**

`float64` has only 53 bits of mantissa precision (~9e15 exact integer range). If `float64(quotaCpu) * ratio.CPURatio` exceeds `math.MaxInt64`, the product becomes `+Inf`, and `int64(+Inf)` on amd64 returns `math.MinInt64`. Even without overflow, values above 2^53 lose integer precision during the float conversion.

Consider clamping the result:

```suggestion
func (s *SchedulerConf) EffectiveQuotaCpu(instanceType string, quotaCpu int64) int64 {
	ratio := s.GetEffectiveOvercommitRatio(instanceType)
	result := float64(quotaCpu) * ratio.CPURatio
	if result > math.MaxInt64 || math.IsNaN(result) {
		return math.MaxInt64
	}
	if result < 0 {
		return 0
	}
	return int64(result)
}
```
(Same pattern for `EffectiveQuotaMem`)

