body:
**`contextReader.Read` doesn't check context before the first I/O call**

In the `select` statement on lines 175-179, the `default` case immediately calls `r.r.Read(p)`. If the context was already cancelled before this `Read` call, the code still performs the I/O operation (up to 32 KiB via `io.Copy`'s internal buffer) before noticing.

**Recommendation**: Add a pre-check:
```go
func (r contextReader) Read(p []byte) (int, error) {
    if err := r.ctx.Err(); err != nil {
        return 0, err
    }
    select {
    case <-r.ctx.Done():
        return 0, r.ctx.Err()
    default:
        return r.r.Read(p)
    }
}
```

