body:
**Sequential envd init blocks sandbox creation on a best-effort side-effect.** The `init_sandbox_env_vars` call on line 179 is awaited inline, adding up to 10s of latency (per `ENVD_INIT_TIMEOUT_SECS`) to every sandbox creation request that includes env vars. Yet lines 180-185 already treat failure as non-fatal (logged at WARN, sandbox creation still succeeds).

Since the call is already best-effort, spawning it as a `tokio::spawn` background task would eliminate this latency from the critical path without changing any semantics. The `SandboxService` is already `Clone` so `self.clone()` can be used inside the spawned task.

```rust
if let Some(env_vars) = env_vars {
    let this = self.clone();
    let sid = resp.sandbox_id.clone();
    tokio::spawn(async move {
        if let Err(err) = this.init_sandbox_env_vars(&sid, &env_vars).await {
            tracing::warn!(sandbox_id = %sid, error = %err, "envd init after create failed");
        }
    });
}
```

